    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4fefed2d_2ff28e87",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanRenderPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 28
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T15:42:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "See my response to your other comment (https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/946877/comment/f88a59a4_9b3e8299/), but no, there are still technically instances where we do not expect to have an input attachment on the main subpass. \n\nYou had commented on whether we wanted to add the subpass self-dependency for all RPs or just those w/ input attachments (https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/946877/comment/7b25983a_55f3cfd7/), and I think it made sense to only do so when we have an input attachment and modified that accordinly.\n\nWe *could* have RPs always have one even in cases where the dst texture read strategy is not ReadFromInput, as will eventually be the case when we can read dst MSAA textures (assuming we always expect to have input attachment usage on dst textures). LMKWYT; I can also add a comment at some key spots that this will eventually always be true (again, given the dst texture will be assumed to have input attachment usage OR we just have an input attachment anyway that simply goes unused in cases where it does not).",
      "parentUuid": "18335a48_b8c81bc2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "eb974d20f7c5c20b5ca693b58e9a5288c64e88f8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eac50715_791d944d",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanRenderPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 28
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-05T18:48:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think our end goal is that all color attachments we use (created by us or wrapped from client) will require input usage. So in an ideal world we would just always bind an input attachment and the depenedecy every time. Also our only real focus for this in Android, though having other platforms work is nice for testing purposes.\n\nI guess there is an open question if there are platforms where you explicitly cannot set input usage on an msaa texture.",
      "parentUuid": "4fefed2d_2ff28e87",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "eb974d20f7c5c20b5ca693b58e9a5288c64e88f8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "060465f0_0da91395",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanRenderPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 28
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-06T20:11:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My initial digging doesn\u0027t point towards such a limitation existing. \n\nWith that being the case, I now have every renderpass support reading the dst as an input attachment even if the rp\u0027s dst read strategy is not `kReadFromInput`. The command buffer now assumes this as well for texture layout purposes, though will still only update + bind a real input attachment descriptor for this usage when the *pipeline* reports it will be used (at which point we know definitively that one will actually be used). That last bit of work is in the follow-on CL.\n\nThe only \"con\" to this is that this will technically be doing a small amount of extra work for such cases until we can read from msaa textures as input attachments as well (b/390458117). Added a comment note for this (wasn\u0027t sure of the best placement though).",
      "parentUuid": "eac50715_791d944d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "eb974d20f7c5c20b5ca693b58e9a5288c64e88f8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60c88e60_b2d3c551",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanRenderPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 28
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-07T18:37:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per offline discussion - I returned to considering whether may read from the dst (as in, we use an input attachment on the main subpass) for layout decisions.\n\nAs it is right now, the subpass dependency regardless / in all cases. Though TBH that doesn\u0027t provide us much of anything, seeing as whether or not we have an input attachment on the main subpass (i.e., when a render target can be sampled from as an input attachment) already makes those RP keys different from other ones. That being said, it always being present is convenient for some logic I suppose (and is basically free as discussed). **LMK if you have thoughts on whether the addition of that self-dependency should also be determined by whether or not the dst can be read as input attachment.** I could see an argument for returning to having this be conditional.\n\nSo, as it stands, any renderpass that *can* read from the dst as an input attachment can be shared for draws that do read from the dst and those that do not. Though RPs that cannot use the dst texture as an input attachment will be distinct (since the attachment indices differ at the subpass level which is part of the key - we can\u0027t point the main subpass\u0027s input attachment to the color attachment if it does not have the proper usage). Does this align with your expectations?",
      "parentUuid": "060465f0_0da91395",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "eb974d20f7c5c20b5ca693b58e9a5288c64e88f8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e3cd50f9_5e788542",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/vk/VulkanRenderPass.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 28
      },
      "lineNbr": 186,
      "author": {
        "id": 18914
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-26T15:52:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Okay, after much offline turmoil and wrestling with validation layers and layout performance concerns , here is where we landed (working on doc, but here is the gist. Comment docs have been added at key areas in an attempt to explain the choices made):\n\nCompatible-only RPS:\n- always have the main subpass self-dependency (necessary for compatibility; neglibile performance cost)\n- always assign the main subpass\u0027s input attachment to point to the color attachment (necessary for compatibility)\n- always use VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_GENERAL for the color and input attachment references on the main subpass (necessary to avoid validation layer complaints even on compatible-only RPs)\n\nFull RPs that do have NO draws which read from the dst as an input attachment (including those that do texture copies, which right now is necessary for MSAA target textures):\n- Use VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_COLOR_ATTACHMENT_OPTIMAL for color attachment reference\n- Assign a different key value at for the main subpass\u0027s input attachment reference (arbitrarily the statically-defined kAttachmentUnused, even though we cannot actually utilize VK_ATTACHMENT_UNUSED for the input attachment reference without violating RP compatibility)\n- Still use VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_GENERAL for the input attachment reference, though drivers supposedly are able to optimize around this and thusly should not impact the more common case of no-dst-read RPs using optimal layouts)\n\nFull RPs that DO read from the dst as an input attachment:\n- Are simply a full versions of the compatible-only RPs that are used for pipeline compilations (those that do and do not read from the dst)",
      "parentUuid": "60c88e60_b2d3c551",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 186,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 186,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "eb974d20f7c5c20b5ca693b58e9a5288c64e88f8",
